# Ticket Manager — Project Memory

## Stack
- GNOME Shell extension (42+), GJS, St widgets, Clutter
- Single-file architecture in `extension.js`
- CSS styling via `stylesheet.css`
- Data persisted as JSON files in `~/.local/share/gnome-shell/extensions/ticket-manager@support.tech/`

## Key Rules

### JS / Shell API
- `const Main = imports.ui.main` (NOT destructuring `{ Main } = imports.ui`)
- `init()` returns nothing (undefined); top-level `enable()`/`disable()` control lifecycle
- `menu.box.add_actor()` instead of `menu.addActor()`
- `St.IconType` does NOT exist — omit `iconType` from St.Icon props
- `St.Label.set_tooltip_text()` not available — use `St.Button` with `set_tooltip_text`
- ModalDialog from `imports.ui.modalDialog`
- `ExtensionUtils.getSettings()` looks up schema via `settings-schema` key in `metadata.json`
- `Clutter.ModifierType.CONTROL_MASK` (not `Clutter.CONTROL_MASK`)

### Shortcut (Alt+T)
- Registered via `Main.wm.addKeybinding()` with `Shell.ActionMode.NORMAL | Shell.ActionMode.SYSTEM_MODAL`
- GSettings schema: `toggle-shortcut`, type `as`, default `['<Alt>t']`
- Schema file: `schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.ticket-manager.gschema.xml`
- Needs `glib-compile-schemas schemas/` after changes

### Lifecycle
- `enable()` creates TicketIndicator, adds to panel, registers shortcut
- `disable()` unregisters shortcut, destroys indicator
- On reload: `disable()` → `enable()`

### Storage
- `var Storage` defined as `{load, save, add, remove, removeAll, update}`
- `const storage = Storage;` must appear AFTER `var Storage` definition (JS hoisting)
- Data files: `tickets.json` + `settings.json`
- Path: `GLib.build_filenamev([GLib.get_user_data_dir(), Me.uuid])`

### Ticket Data Model
```js
{
  id: string,       // optional, blank if omitted
  title: '',        // unused (field removed)
  url: string,
  status: string,    // one of: onhold, answered, in_progress, closed, sales_billing
  createdAt: timestamp,
  updatedAt: timestamp
}
```
Stored extra fields (priority, category, assignee, tags, description) from original model are preserved by `Storage.add()` but not exposed in UI.

### Status Values
| Key             | Label          | CSS class       | Color  |
|-----------------|----------------|-----------------|--------|
| `onhold`        | On Hold        | `status-onhold` | #3584e4 (blue) |
| `answered`      | Answered       | `status-answered` | #ffffff (white) |
| `in_progress`   | In Progress    | `status-in_progress` | #c01c28 (red) |
| `closed`        | Closed         | `status-closed` | #26a269 (green) |
| `sales_billing` | Sales/Billing  | `status-sales_billing` | #e5a50a (yellow) |

### UI Architecture (popup menu layout)
```
Header: [Title "Ticket Manager"] [stats] [spacer] [gear icon]
Search: [entry box]
List:   [ScrollView > ticket rows (ID + URL vertical | status | edit | delete)]
Add:    [inline form — replaces search+list when "+ Add" clicked]
Footer: [Delete All] [spacer] [+ Add]
```

### Ticket Row Layout
```
[ticket-row]
  [leftBlock: vertical]
    [id metadata label]
    [url label — clickable, reactive, auto-ellipsis via x_expand]
  [spacer: x_expand]
  [status label — colored badge]
  [edit button — pencil icon]
  [delete button — trash icon]
```

### Ticket Row Rules
- URL is `St.Label` (NOT `St.Button`) with `reactive: true` — auto-ellipsis via `x_expand: true` avoids horizontal scroll
- LeftBlock uses `x_expand: true` + spacer widget for width distribution
- ID label uses `ticket-id-metadata` style (small, gray, monospace)
- Edit button opens ModalDialog (pencil icon)
- Delete button removes directly + re-renders (trash icon)

### Add Form (inline, no modal)
- Hidden by default; `_showAddForm()` hides search + list, shows form
- Fields: ID (optional), URL (required), status buttons, Cancel, Create
- `_hideAddForm()` hides form, shows search + list
- Status buttons are `inline-opt-btn` with `selected` class for active

### Settings Panel
- Accessed via gear icon in header
- Sections: Width stepper, Keyboard Shortcut (read-only `<Alt>T`), Copyright
- Width persisted in `settings.json`, range 280–700px, step 20
- Copyright: `© Karthik | github.com/karthik-ka`

### Dialogs (both use ModalDialog)
1. **Edit dialog** — ID/URL/status changes via `Storage.update(id, changes)`
2. **Delete All confirmation** — `Storage.removeAll()`

### CSS Conventions
- Adwaita dark theme colors: backgrounds `#353535`, borders `#5e5c64`, text `#ffffff`
- All in `stylesheet.css` — no theme overrides
- Status label CSS: `.status-label` base + `.status-{key}` color class

## Files

### extension.js (~674 lines)
All logic inline: indicator, popup menu, ticket rows, add form, settings, storage.

### stylesheet.css (~433 lines)
All St widget styling including status colors, buttons, forms, settings.

### metadata.json
- uuid: `ticket-manager@support.tech`
- shell-version: 42, 43, 44, 45, 46
- settings-schema: `org.gnome.shell.extensions.ticket-manager`

### schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.ticket-manager.gschema.xml
Key: `toggle-shortcut` (type `as`, default `['<Alt>t']`)

### install.sh
One-command installer; uses `SCRIPT_DIR` for path independence.
Copies files, compiles schema, enables extension.
Needs `glib-compile-schemas` (from `glib2` tools).

### Directory
```
ticket-manager@support.tech/
├── extension.js
├── stylesheet.css
├── metadata.json
├── install.sh
├── schemas/
│   ├── org.gnome.shell.extensions.ticket-manager.gschema.xml
│   └── gschemas.compiled
```

## Install Commands
```bash
mkdir -p ~/.local/share/gnome-shell/extensions/ticket-manager@support.tech
cp extension.js stylesheet.css metadata.json -t <dest>
cp -r schemas <dest>/
glib-compile-schemas <dest>/schemas/
gnome-extensions enable ticket-manager@support.tech
```
Then `Alt+F2` → `r` → Enter.

## Known Issues / Pitfalls
- `const storage = Storage;` must be AFTER `var Storage = { ... }` (JS hoisting)
- URL uses `St.Label` (not `St.Button`) to avoid horizontal scrollbar
- Shortcut uses `Shell.ActionMode.NORMAL | Shell.ActionMode.SYSTEM_MODAL` because popup menu pushModal sets SYSTEM_MODAL
- Alt-modified key events are intercepted by Mutter WM; WM keybinding is the only reliable way to catch them (stage handler would NOT work)
- `PopupMenu` import must NOT be used (causes errors)
- No `iconType` prop on `St.Icon` (doesn't exist in this GNOME version)
